# Read-only drawing policy for the pilot/LLM.
#
# Call this before planning a drawing request: it exposes the switches
# that decide whether a preview is available (debug) and whether
# text-to-image is usable (imagegen_ready). It never moves the machine and
# never writes files.
#
# Planning rules:
#   structured/geometric request:
#       plotter_home -> render_preview (debug=true only) -> scene
#   free-form/illustrative request with imagegen_ready=true:
#       plotter_home -> prompt
#       on failure: author a simple declarative scene and use scene
#   Preview failures never block drawing.
#
# plotter_home and render_preview are separate tool calls. Pass
# skip_home=true / skip_preview=true to the draw tool when those steps
# were already performed, so the skill does not repeat them.
---
bool    success
string  message
# render_preview is enabled and scene writes the preview PNG itself.
bool    debug
# prompt is enabled in the skill config.
bool    imagegen_enabled
# prompt has everything it needs (enabled + base URL + model).
bool    imagegen_ready
string  image_dir
string  output_dir
# Fixed name used for manual and automatic previews inside output_dir.
string  preview_name
# Draw tools run the primitive HOME routine before moving.
bool    home_before_draw
float64 elapsed_s